claimed: okay-script-cookie-flags -- found while answering 'what goes to the proxy' (operator, 2026-09-07): the session cookie is set HttpOnly; Path=/ with NO Secure and NO SameSite, and Response.current.cookie cannot express either -- a cookie without Secure leaves on a plaintext request, one without SameSite rides cross-site. Adds `secure` and `sameSite` to api.Response.cookie (SameSite=Lax the default, because a session cookie that rides a cross-site POST is the CSRF surface); Site gains secureCookies: Option[Boolean] = None -- None means DECIDE per request (our own TLS, or X-Forwarded-Proto: https from a trusted proxy when Site(trustForwarded = true)), Some(b) forces it. The OKAYLANG cookie gets the same treatment. Serve reads OKAY_FORWARDED=1. Tests through Site.handle over http, over https, and behind a forwarded header both trusted and not.
